# The six countries at their hearts and the land turning at three borders,
# on seed 1 at a clear late morning, each with a short real walk.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/countries.tour --seed=1 --hour=10.5 --weather=clear:0
#
# Every heart is asked for BY NAME. `place coast` is GenPlaces.country_sample,
# which scores a standing tile by how much of its own country surrounds it at
# 6, 12, 20 and 30 tiles — so it IS the heart, by definition, in whatever world
# it is asked in. These six lines used to be six numbers copied off one
# `tools/map.sh --seed=1` run, and four of the six had quietly stopped being
# what the run said they were:
#   coast     338,398 sat at blend 0.36 — deep in an ECOTONE band. A frame
#             called "coast-heart" was a picture of a border. See the note on
#             its line below: it is the one place here still on a coordinate.
#   moss      262,242 was on GRAVEL, 47 tiles off the sample. (Now 266,290, moss.)
#   pinewood  362,222 had no PINE within nine tiles. (Now 366,222, four of them.)
#   bonelands 138,242 was a RIVERBED. (Now 134,254, limestone pavement under
#             clints, which is what the bonelands are.)
# The snowfield and the burning still resolve to the very tiles that were
# written down, so those two frames do not move at all — which is the point: a
# name costs nothing when nothing has changed and fixes itself when it has.
coast calm
# THE COAST IS THE ONE HEART STILL ON A COORDINATE, and it is the only frame in
# this file taken on the strength of what it LOOKS like rather than what it is
# called. Three tiles were shot and looked at:
#   338,398    what was here. Blend 0.36 — an ecotone. A frame named for one
#              landscape showing two, with a stone circle in the middle of it.
#   250,406    `place coast`, which is GenPlaces.country_sample and therefore
#              the coast's heartland by construction. On seed 1 that lands
#              twenty tiles off the plan's Turf Rows depot, and the picture is
#              masts, wire, a fire tower and cleared earth. Honest about the
#              tile, wrong about the subject: a photograph of a depot that
#              happens to stand on the coast (owner's ruling).
#   110,436    this. Turf terraces stepping down to a sand bay, the sun on the
#              water, boulders, driftwood, broadleaf wood behind, and one fallen
#              pylon truss for the machines. No village, no depot, no landmark.
#
# A search of the whole island says seed 1 holds 740 tiles like the third: coast,
# blend 0, at least 30 from any depot, 22 from any village, 16 from any landmark,
# with the sea within nine. So the coast is not short of heartland — what is
# missing is a NAME for it. Every name GenPlaces knows that reaches the coast is
# the spawn, the country sample, or a landmark, and a landmark in frame is the
# same objection as the depot.
#
# So this number stays until the new GenPlaces key for open ground in a landscape
# lands, and then it goes. TWO THINGS THAT KEY MUST DO for this frame, which are
# not in its brief as written: clear LANDMARKS as well as villages and works, or
# it can still resolve to the lighthouse; and prefer a tile with the landscape's
# own character in shot, which on the coast means the strand — the highest-scoring
# open tile on this island by prop count alone is a reed marsh.
# `prop:driftwood` is what guards it in the meantime: the frame has to hold the
# strand, so a worldgen change that moves the shoreline out of it fails the tour
# rather than filing a field under the name "coast-heart".
# By name since GEN 24 moved every seed's coast: the coast, then its strand.
place coast
near driftwood
wait 2.0
shot 01-coast-heart with land:coast,prop:driftwood
walk 0,-1 1.2
shot 02-coast-walked with land:coast
place moss
wait 2.0
shot 03-moss-heart with land:moss
place pinewood
wait 2.0
shot 04-pinewood-heart with land:pinewood
place snowfield
wait 2.0
shot 05-snowfield-heart with land:snowfield
place bonelands
wait 2.0
shot 06-bonelands-heart with land:bonelands
place burning
wait 2.0
shot 07-burning-heart with land:burning
# Borders: stand in the band, then walk across it. The band is asked for by
# name, not pinned to a coordinate: 307,355 was copied off a map run once and is
# coast heartland now, so `08-coast-moss` was a picture of the coast alone.
place coast-moss
wait 2.0
shot 08-coast-moss with border:coast-moss
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
shot 09-coast-moss-crossed with land:coast|moss
# Borders this seed holds. Which landscapes meet is the layout's, and the layout
# moves: the snowfield met the mesas and the Burning once and on seed 1 today
# meets only the salt flats and the grey orchards (a scan of every tile's pair,
# 2026-09-26, the same on main). A border named here that the seed no longer
# holds fails at `place`, which is the right way for it to fail.
place snowfield-salt_flats
wait 2.0
shot 10-snowfield-salt_flats with border:snowfield-salt_flats
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
shot 11-snowfield-salt_flats-crossed with land:snowfield|salt_flats
place snowfield-grey_orchards
wait 2.0
shot 12-snowfield-grey_orchards with border:snowfield-grey_orchards
walk 1,-1 2.5 run
shot 13-snowfield-grey_orchards-crossed with land:snowfield|grey_orchards
